Although \LaTeX\ is widely used in academia and education, only a few
developers use it to create \PDF{}s in web applications or \acro{IT} systems.
This seems strange considering that many developers are well exposed to
these academic and scientific milieux \Dash and that many recognize \LaTeX\
for its superior typesetting qualities.

In this paper, we try to answer two questions:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Why use of \LaTeX\ in \acro{IT} systems is not widespread \Dash and
    not even common?
    \item How can we change this state of affairs?
\end{itemize}

In this article we give an overview of LaTeX-on-\HTTP\
(\tbsurl{github.com/YtoTech/latex-on-http}), an attempt to commodify and
simplify \LaTeX\ use in web applications or \acro{IT} systems, and to
ease its adoption by modern developers.
